g now because they had  close contact with marlin humphrey but  but i the only reason i bring a lot of  this up  is that  look  sunday i wouldn't call it a must win but  it's damn close for the baltimore ravens  they are at indianapolis coming off  another bad big game  by lamar jackson okay  and and and so on sunday they're playing  a team in the indianapolis colts who's  got who got their act together on  offense phillip rivers one turnover in  the last two weeks 113 quarterback  rating  he is he's  you know seemingly on right now you've  got to play very well and you've got  basically now going up against the  number two defense in football  and  so you've got to lean on this offense to  be the real big factor in this game  because you really don't have much of an  idea how is their defense going to play  when they haven't been together the  whole week the entire week mike not just  a few days they have not practiced once  as a defense the entire week and so you  have to ask yourself the question  how much is kovit going to damage the  baltimore ravens  this would have been a good week to have  a gimme game  this is not a gimme game in indianapolis  on sunday  yeah but i still have faith in john  harbaugh and company to coach up the  guys they have to make sure their guys  are ready it isn't going to be easy  and and look 265 rushing yards against  the pittsburgh steelers last week i  think the ravens have plenty of reasons  to feel good about their offense coming  out of that game i agree lamar jackson  can't play like that on a regular basis  it's going to be impossible to win  consistently if he does  but between j.k dobbins and gus edwards  and lamar jackson cranking up the  yardage they did if they can do that  again it's not going to be any easier  against the colts defense than it was  against the steelers but they still  pulled it off i've got faith in the  ravens but it is a difficult situation  and it's one of these  byproducts of one positive that you 